  "text": "Open Shortcuts on the toolbar. Press the binding you want to change, then press the key, remote or pedal you want; Escape leaves it as it was. Search by a command's name or by the key itself. If two commands share a key, both rows say so; clear one with ×, or choose Restore defaults. Most foot pedals and presenter remotes send ordinary keys, usually F13 to F24, so they bind with no driver and no setup. Bindings follow the physical key, not the letter printed on it, so they survive a change of keyboard layout. The Anywhere column asks your system to deliver a key even when another app is in front — a camera app, a DAW or OBS. Nothing is claimed until you set it, and a key another program already owns says so. Under Wayland on Linux, apps cannot claim keys system-wide, and the dialog tells you. While you are writing, the space bar, the arrow keys and Home type as normal: a bare key runs its command only outside the editor."
